                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#holographic"} Holographic
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phases+of+matter"} phases
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+physics"} quantum materials
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gapped+Hamiltonian"} gapped Hamiltonian
            admit a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"}> topological
            ” (really:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theoretical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+states+of+matter"} topological states of matter
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulators"} topological insulators
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#holographic_relation_to_ktheory_classification_of_dbrane_charge Holographic relation to K-theory classification of D-brane charge
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality+in+solid+state+physics"} AdS/CFT duality in solid state physics
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
            corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} K-theory classification of D-brane charge
            (
            %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi10a"}> Ryu-Takayanagi 10a
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi10b"} Ryu-Takayanagi 10v
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+topological+phases+of+matter"} unstable topological phases of matter
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} K-theory classification of D-brane charge
          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#topological_phases_of_matter_via_ktheory Topological phases of matter via K-theory
            %h4#for_freefermion_topological_insulators For free-fermion topological insulators
            %p
              On the classification (now often referred to, somewhat rudimentarily, as the
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ten-fold+way"} ten-fold way
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field"} free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+physics"} condensed matter
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gapped+Hamiltonians"} gapped Hamiltonians
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulators"} topological insulators
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %p
              Early detailed discussion (ignored by the revival of the idea following
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Kitaev09"} Kitaev 2009
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Bellissard"}> Jean Bellissard
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    K-theory of
                    = succeed "-Algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Statistical mechanics and field theory: Mathematical Aspects
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 2577
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => " https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-16777-3_74"} doi:10.1007/3-540-16777-3_74
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/222243"} inSpire:222243
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://lib-extopc.kek.jp/preprints/PDF/1986/8604/8604219.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              Later precursor discussion phrased in terms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+matrix+theory"} random matrix theory
              instead of K-theory:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Denis Bernard, André LeClair,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A classification of 2D random Dirac fermions
                  %strong 35
                  (2002) 2555 [
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/0305-4470/35/11/303"}> doi:10.1088/0305-4470/35/11/303
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+P.+Schnyder"}> Andreas P. Schnyder
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinsei+Ryu"} Shinsei Ryu
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Furusaki"} Akira Furusaki
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+W.+W.+Ludwig"} Andreas W. W. Ludwig
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Classification of topological insulators and superconductors in three spatial dimensions
                  %strong 78
                  195125 (2008)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.78.195125"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.78.195125
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0803.2786"} arXiv:0803.2786
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              The original proposal making
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              explicit:
            %ul
              %li#Kitaev09
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Kitaev"}> Alexei Kitaev
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Periodic table for topological insulators and superconductors
                %p
                  AIP Conference Proceedings 1134 (2009) 22-30 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.3149495"}> doi:10.1063/1.3149495
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.2686"} arXiv:0901.2686
            %p Further details:
            %p
              The technical part of the argument always essentially boils down (implicitly, never attributed this way before
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#FreedMoore13"} Freed &amp; Moore 2013
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+K-theory"} Karoubi K-theory
              from:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Index theory for skew-adjoint Fredholm operators
                  %strong 37
                  (1969) 5-26
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/PMIHES_1969__37__5_0"} numdam:PMIHES_1969__37__5_0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Espaces Classifiants en K-Théorie
                  %strong 147
                  1 (Jan., 1970) 75-115
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1995218"} doi:10.2307/1995218
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              More on this
              = succeed "-argument" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Michael Stone, Ching-Kai Chiu, Abhishek Roy,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Symmetries, dimensions and topological insulators: the mechanism behind the face of the Bott clock
                  %strong 44
                  4 (2010) 045001
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1751-8113/44/4/045001"} doi:10.1088/1751-8113/44/4/045001
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  Gilles Abramovici, Pavel Kalugin,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Clifford modules and symmetries of topological insulators
                  %strong 09
                  03 (2012) 1250023
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1101.1054"} arXiv:1101.1054
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0219887812500235"} doi:10.1142/S0219887812500235
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              The proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
              formulation expected to apply also to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+crystalline+insulators"} topological crystalline insulators
            %ul
              %li#FreedMoore13
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twisted equivariant matter
                %strong 14
                (2013) 1927-2023
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.5055"} arXiv:1208.5055
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00023-013-0236-x"} doi:10.1007/s00023-013-0236-x
            %p Further discussion:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guo+Chuan+Thiang"}> Guo Chuan Thiang
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the K-theoretic classification of topological phases of matter
                  %strong 17
                  4 (2016) 757-794 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00023-015-0418-9"}> doi:10.1007/s00023-015-0418-9
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.7366"} arXiv:1406.7366
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guo+Chuan+Thiang"}> Guo Chuan Thiang
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Topological phases: isomorphism, homotopy and K-theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.4191"} arXiv:1412.4191
